1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,049
In France, every restaurant inspection ends with a public grade.

2
00:00:04,049 --> 00:00:06,328
The worst one can close you for weeks.

3
00:00:06,328 --> 00:00:10,143
Most owners find out what's wrong the day the inspector walks in.

4
00:00:10,143 --> 00:00:13,372
A pre-inspection audit costs a few hundred euros.

5
00:00:13,372 --> 00:00:15,833
The businesses that need it most never call.

6
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:17,252
Argus is that audit.

7
00:00:17,252 --> 00:00:19,140
From a phone, in a minute.

8
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:23,281
Built on NVIDIA Nemotron, running on Nebius Token Factory.

9
00:00:23,281 --> 00:00:24,895
You photograph the kitchen.

10
00:00:24,895 --> 00:00:28,697
Fridges, surfaces, the dish area, the floor.

11
00:00:28,697 --> 00:00:30,520
You say what photos can't show.

12
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:32,695
You paste your temperature log as it is.

13
00:00:32,695 --> 00:00:35,703
A notebook, a spreadsheet, a text message.

14
00:00:35,703 --> 00:00:37,552
And you describe your situation.

15
00:00:37,552 --> 00:00:39,218
Now watch the agent work.

16
00:00:39,218 --> 00:00:44,335
A vision model reads each photo like an inspector would, with a confidence score.

17
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:49,388
Nemotron Nano turns your voice note into facts and transcribes the logbook.

18
00:00:49,388 --> 00:00:56,549
Then a rule engine, not a model, applies the legal limits and spots the fridge that's been drifting for three days.

19
00:00:56,549 --> 00:01:05,494
Finally, Nemotron Ultra, five hundred and fifty billion parameters, cross-checks every piece of evidence against the official inspection grid.

20
00:01:05,494 --> 00:01:07,005
Thirty-eight seconds.

21
00:01:07,005 --> 00:01:09,466
Here's the grade the inspector would publish.

22
00:01:09,466 --> 00:01:11,354
And the rule that leads to it.

23
00:01:11,354 --> 00:01:16,692
Every finding cites the grid point, the regulation, the proof, and the deadline.

24
00:01:16,692 --> 00:01:18,385
The stews cooled overnight?

25
00:01:18,385 --> 00:01:19,231
Critical.

26
00:01:19,231 --> 00:01:20,468
Point B seven.

27
00:01:20,468 --> 00:01:21,731
Immediate action.

28
00:01:21,731 --> 00:01:23,541
No photo could have shown that.

29
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:26,015
The kitchen map tells you where it hurts.

30
00:01:26,015 --> 00:01:30,651
The evidence gallery shows exactly what the model saw, and how sure it was.

31
00:01:30,651 --> 00:01:33,697
What it couldn't see goes to "to verify on site".

32
00:01:33,697 --> 00:01:35,742
No finding without evidence.

33
00:01:35,742 --> 00:01:39,622
One more click, and Nemotron Super writes your food safety plan.

34
00:01:39,622 --> 00:01:42,708
The document the law requires, for this kitchen.

35
00:01:42,708 --> 00:01:51,770
Hygiene practices, HACCP control points, records, and a thirty-day action plan where every action points back to the finding it fixes.

36
00:01:51,770 --> 00:01:53,658
Export it as a PDF.

37
00:01:53,658 --> 00:01:55,963
Models perceive and extract.

38
00:01:55,963 --> 00:01:57,200
Code decides.

39
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:02,864
Four Nemotron calls, one rule engine, one reference written from the real inspection grid.

40
00:02:02,864 --> 00:02:06,458
Open source, Apache two point zero, live today.

41
00:02:06,458 --> 00:02:07,356
Argus.

42
00:02:07,356 --> 00:02:09,882
See your kitchen the way the inspector will.

43
00:02:09,882 --> 00:02:11,145
Before it matters.

